# A running turn on a 30-column pane, as claude 2.1.259 draws it. The spinner
# row is a glyph, a gerund, an ellipsis and a parenthesis with the elapsed time
# and a detail; claude drops that tail from the right as the pane narrows, and
# at this width all of it is gone.
#
# No hooks: a reader looks at the screen once hooks stop (after Escape, or an
# agent gone quiet), and claude draws the mode footer while working too, so the
# spinner row alone must tell a running turn from a finished one.
print ● Finagling… thinking
print ──────────────────────────────
print ❯
print ──────────────────────────────
print   ⏵⏵ auto mode on
# The turn runs until the test ends it.
sleep 600000
